# Python Environment Setup

Before running any Python code, tests, or scripts in this project, always use the virtual environment defined in your local dev config (`scripts/.prepare_commit.cfg`).

## One-time developer setup

If you haven't already, copy the example config and fill in your package manager and environment name:

```bash
cp scripts/.prepare_commit.cfg.example scripts/.prepare_commit.cfg
```

## Activating your environment

Use the `package_manager` and `env_name` values from your `scripts/.prepare_commit.cfg`:

| package_manager | Activation command |
|---|---|
| `conda` | `conda activate <env_name>` |
| `venv` / `virtualenv` | `source <env_name>/bin/activate` |
| `poetry` | `poetry shell` |
| `pipenv` | `pipenv shell` |

Then install the project in editable mode:

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Shell Commands

Always prefix terminal commands so the correct environment is used:

```bash
# conda example
conda run -n <env_name> <your command>

# venv/virtualenv example
source <env_name>/bin/activate && <your command>

# poetry example
poetry run <your command>

# pipenv example
pipenv run <your command>
```
